  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Stacked on #649** (#637 step B), which is stacked on #646 (step A). Merge them in that order. This is **#637 step C**, the clip from the design comment on #637.\n\n`CarriedField` gains an optional **clip block** in the new frame.\n- **The law:** the carried solid is **intersected** with the later setup's own stock block, `distance = max(d_body, d_block)`, and membership is body **and** block. That's the field's form of the column body's `lower()` clip in `stock_sim_carry`.\n- **A second clip** narrows the block; it never widens it.\n- **Carrying again** (`then`) carries the clip through the same turn.\n- **New `box_signed(lo, hi, p)`:** the exact signed distance to an axis-aligned box (negative inside), re-exported from `stock_sim`.\n- **Not yet wired:** nothing uses it yet. That's step D, the `Body` enum and its agreement lane.\n\nIt merges step B's review fix: the 3×3×3 near-tool floor refusal.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **`crates/sim/tests/field_carry.rs`, 5/5** (3 from step A plus 2 new):\n  - `a_clip_intersects_the_carried_solid_with_the_next_block`: at every sample the clipped distance is exactly `max(body, block)` and membership is `body && block`. A second clip only narrows.\n  - `box_signed_is_negative_inside_and_euclidean_outside`: inside (−1), outside (3), a 3-4-5 corner (5) and on a face (0).\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** the sim suites pass. Named: field_floor 3 (after the merge), stock_backend_parity 13, stock_columns 3, and app setup_carry 9, carried_verify 8.\n- **Clippy** on sim with `-D warnings`: clean. No golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nStep D (the body enum with its carried-verdict agreement lane) and step E (the app holders), per #637.\n\nChangelog: none (internal: a clip for the carried field, not yet used)\n\nRefs #637\nRefs #26\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
